returns 'unverified' (line 14). `providerStatus(config, opts={})` (line 33) passes opts through. No way to inject a fake spawn/exec; real subprocess always runs with `shell: process.platform === 'win32'` (line 5).\n- select.mjs: `cliCall` (line 35) builds command strings from config; pure function, no exec. `selectModels(config, request, {status, usage})` (line 75) — status is injectable as plain data, usage as records array. So selection is pure and already testable (tests do this). But forecast is called 3x per model (lines 94, 102, 116) — no inject counter.\n- forecast.mjs: `forecast({..., now = Date.now()})` (line 17) — `now` IS injectable (clock seam) — the only real DI seam. But uses `Date.parse` (line 20) internally, not injectable. No fs/fetch.\n- cli.mjs: direct `fs`, `path` (lines 1-2), `process.argv` (lines 10-11, 19-20), `process.stdout/stderr` (lines 8-9), `new Date().toISOString()` (line 53). No injection; `main()` called at module load (line 65) — hard to import without executing. `fail()` calls process.exit (line 9).\n- config.mjs: `loadConfig({file})` (line 11) — file path injectable via param + `process.env.CLIWORKER_CONFIG`/`CLIWORKER_HOME` (lines 8, 12). fs is direct singleton (readFileSync line 14, appendFileSync line 35). readUsage/appendUsage take a `file` param (lines 27, 33) — path injectable but fs not. env vars are global mutable — a config-path seam exists but no fs abstraction.\n- No `fetch` anywhere (grep confirmed). No direct `exec` (only spawnSync). No dependency-injection container.\n\n3. test/ helpers/fixtures/mocks:\n- Only one test file: test/select.test.mjs (86 lines). Uses node:test + assert/strict. Builds an inline `config()` object literal (lines 9-24). Imports fs, os, path but NEVER uses them (lines 3-5 — unused imports, relevant to check-unused). No fake CLI, no shim generator, no fs probe, no mocks, no fixtures dir. status passed as plain object (line 27). Globs for test/helpers, test/fixtures returned nothing.\n\n4. Env/to