{"type":"user","uuid":"01a1b5a7-fac0-7862-a058-441619ed9aa5","session_id":"01a1b5a4-00dc-7683-9b43-241448a2c172","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-827575f7ba1d9f17","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Findings (read-only; Bash/PowerShell execution was sandbox-denied, so `pwsh`/`node` probes could not run — Q4 is file-detectable only)\n\n**1. `lib/index.js` (DSH plugin)**\nExports: `name='cliworker'` (`lib/index.js:40`) and `apply(ctx, config={})` (`lib/index.js:42`). Settings merge `DEFAULTS={configPath, readonly}` (`lib/index.js:19-22,43`); `configPath` from `CLIWORKER_CONFIG`/`CLIWORKER_HOME`. Host API the plugin expects (undocumented, implicit): `ctx.inject(['webServer'], cb)` → `httpCtx.effect(() => httpCtx.webServer.register({kind:'exact',path,handler}), name)` (`lib/index.js:47-48`). Routes: `/cliworker/providers|models|select|forecast` (`lib/index.js:50-70`) using Node `req/res` (`send`/`readBody`, `lib/index.js:24-38`). `apply()` wraps everything in try/catch that only `console.error`s (`lib/index.js:46,72-74`) — failures are swallowed, not surfaced. `dsh.plugin.json:5-8` declares `inject: []` (no documented deps); `cordis.patch.yml:1-4` is a bare insert patch; `README.md:40-58` documents only the CLI/`modelSource`. **No contract describes the pseudo-ctx/webServer shape.**\n\n**2. DI seams today (almost none — direct singletons)**\n- `availability.mjs:1` imports `spawnSync` directly; `run()` (`availability.mjs:3-10`) hard-codes `shell: process.platform==='win32'`. Only opt-out is `checkProvider(provider,{probe:false})` → `'unverified'` (`availability.mjs:12-14`). No injectable exec/fake.\n- `config.mjs:1` direct `fs`; `loadConfig({file})` + `CLIWORKER_CONFIG`/`CLIWORKER_HOME` (`config.mjs:11-12`) is the only path seam; `readUsage/appendUsage(file)` (`config.mjs:27,33`) take paths but still use real `fs`.\n- `cli.mjs:1-2,8-11,19-20,53,65`: direct `fs/path`, `process.argv`, stdout/stderr, `new Date()`, and `main()` auto-runs on import (`fail()` calls `process.exit`, `cli.mjs:9`) — hostile to import-based testing.\n- `forecast.mjs:17` — **`now = Date.now()` IS injectable** (the one real seam); `Date.parse` (`forecast.mjs:20`) is not.\n- `select.mjs:75` — `status`/`usage` are injectable plain data (used by tests); but `forecast` is called 3×/model (`select.mjs:94,102,116`), no counter hook. No `fetch`, no DI container anywhere.\n\n**3. test/ infrastructure**\nOnly `test/select.test.mjs` (86 lines): `node:test` + `assert/strict`, inline `config()` literal (`test/select.test.mjs:9-24`), `fs/os/path` imported but unused (`test/select.test.mjs:3-5`). **No fake CLI, shim generator, fs probe, helpers/, fixtures/, or mocks** (globs returned nothing).\n\n**4. Tooling (detectable from files)**\n- `scripts/` absent; no lockfile (no `package-lock.json`/`pnpm-lock.yaml`/`yarn.lock`); no `.nvmrc`/`.node-version`/`.npmrc`.\n- `engines.node=\">=20\"` (`package.json:22-24`). `package.json` has **no `scripts`, no `dependencies`/`devDependencies`** — only built-in `node:test`.\n- `pwsh`/`node --version` not runnable here (commands blocked); `task-graph.json:453` assumes `pwsh`.\n\n**5. Directories**\n`config/` = `cliworker.example.json` only; `test/` = 1 file; `lib/`, `bin/`. **`docs/`, `contracts/`, `ui/`, `scripts/` do not exist.** `.collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/` holds the redesign (`design.md`, `interfaces.md`, `risks.md`, `task-graph.json` = 24 tasks T-001..T-024 / 55 ACs, `state.json`, logs).\n\n**6. Lint/static analysis**\n**None** — no eslint/prettier/biome/tsconfig/.editorconfig (glob: \"No files found\"), no tooling to build `check-unused` on.\n\n## What requires NEW seams/tooling (concrete)\nNearly all: pseudo-ctx/webServer harness (AC-046), injected exec/fake-spawn probes (AC-018/026 — needs new `lib/exec.mjs`, T-008), fake-CLI/shim generator + fs-probe (AC-022, T-011), sentinel-token leak scan (AC-019, needs redact/secrets T-007/009), cross-platform shim removal (AC-016/029 — `shell:true` still at `availability.mjs:5`), timing/concurrency thresholds (AC-017/018), and forecast-once counter (AC-009). Plus all tooling: `scripts/`, lockfile, `check-unused`/`run-tests`/`check-fast.ps1`, `pwsh`. **Already present and reusable:** `now` injection (`forecast.mjs:17`), `status`/`usage` data params (`select.mjs:75`), config-path injection (`config.mjs:11-12`), and built-in `node:test`.\n\n[Agent ID: agent-6c8e587e-c7a0-4ddb-a79b-e5bfb87f30d8]"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a1b5a403737f88a3bc7df5ac6bf66b","_messageId":"01a1b5a40450706f95bcb0794506d404","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a1b5a403737f88a3bc7df5ac6bf66b","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a1b5a40450706f95bcb0794506d404","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a1b5a40450706f95bcb0794506d404","traceparent":"00-83e180a40bd533ed34958179d5cc0dd5-af1d21be7ebe6564-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a1b5a4-00dc-7683-9b43-241448a2c172,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a1b5a403737f88a3bc7df5ac6bf66b"},"__timestamp":"2026-11-07T10:57:27.234Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b5a7-fac5-7791-9bcf-0cc987079d57","session_id":"01a1b5a4-00dc-7683-9b43-241448a2c172","message":{"id":"01a1b5a7fac577919bcf0cc716908711","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have grounded findings. Let me synthesize the test strategy and blockers.\n\nKey grounded facts:\n- package.json: no bin/scripts, files lacks bin/config; type module, engines >=20, zero deps, no lockfile.\n- forecast.mjs: tasks_left only via remaining_usd or unit==='tokens'; otherwise unknown; no samples → early return with no risk key; Number(null)=0 finite edge.\n- select.mjs: 3 call sites (filter, sort comparator 2×, output) — so \"forecast 每模型只算一次\" AC-009 needs a per-model memo, not just \"one call\" (the comparator multiplies). cli and call duplicate; cursor-wsl bash -lc injection.\n- config.mjs: null config TypeError actually from `${raw.schema}` in thrown literal, not the `&&` (the `&&` short-circuits via `!raw`). No _example, no state_dir. usageFile from defaultHome, independent of --config.\n- availability.mjs: spawnSync shell:true win32, 20s timeout, synchronous.\n- cli.mjs: main() auto-runs on import, fail() calls process.exit → import-hostile; no run/resolve/cli command currently; select returns raw provider CLI calls (NOT wrapped run --lease). So the design's \"现状\" claim about wrapped calls is actually a v2 target, not current state — the doc said \"AgentLine 拿到的调用是包装过的\" as a design decision (section 0), which is fine as a target. But the agent flagged \"any claim of a current wrapped run --lease CLI is wrong\" — the design's section 0 is describing the design decision, so it's OK. Still worth noting for test baseline: there is NO current run/lease, so T-019's runner tests are entirely new, not regression.\n- example config quotas: remaining_pct:100/reset_at:null, credits unit:1000, no remaining_usd, no _example, no inline tokens.\n- .gitignore: literal `config/cliworker.local.json`, `usage.jsonl`, `node_modules/` only — does NOT cover `config/*.local.json` glob, `state/`, `*.jsonl` glob.\n- test/: ONE file select.test.mjs, 6 tests, no subdirs, no scripts/, no CI, no lockfile, no lint tooling.\n- Plugin: `apply(ctx, config={})`, expects `ctx.inject(['webServer'], cb)` → `httpCtx.effect(() => httpCtx.webServer.register({kind:'exact',path,handler}), name)`. Node req/res. try/catch swallows errors via console.error. dsh.plugin.json inject:[] — NO documented host contract. This is a real blocker: AC-046 \"用伪 ctx 和 webServer 加载插件\" requires a defined pseudo-ctx/webServer shape; currently implicit and undocumented, and apply() swallows registration failures — a test could pass vacuously. Need to fix: surface errors, define a typed harness/stub.\n- DI seams: almost none. forecast `now` injectable (Date.now), Date.parse not. select status/usage data injectable. config path injectable. cli.mjs auto-runs on import + process.exit → hostile.\n- pwsh not runnable (sandbox denied) — can't confirm availability; task-graph assumes pwsh for AC-002.\n\nNow, let me formulate the test strategy (strategy 正文) and blockers.\n\nAs test architect, my strategy should cover:\n1. Test philosophy & levels mapping to directories, and how run-tests.mjs / check-test-discovery should work.\n2. Grounding in real baseline: the 6 existing tests are the only regression net; need to preserve/migrate them (T-001 moves select.test.mjs to test/unit/) and add characterization tests BEFORE refactoring (A-series fixes), since there are no tests for config/availability/cli/cursor-wsl/null-config. Recommend characterization/golden tests first to lock behavior, then refactor.\n3. Seam-first principle: a cross-cutting requirement — every AC that injects a probe (AC-009 counter, AC-018 exec probe, AC-026 fs probe, AC-046 pseudo ctx, AC-022 fake CLI, AC-019 sentinel) needs an explicit DI seam. Recommend making `lib/exec.mjs`, `lib/store.mjs` accept injectable deps (a single `createContext({exec, fs, now, fetch, env})`), and `cli.mjs` must stop auto-running on import (guard `import.meta.url === ...`). This is the #1 blocker.\n4. Determinism: forbid wall-clock thresholds in CI. AC-017 (N/4+1 s), AC-018 (p95<300ms), AC-048/health — replace with injectable clock + logical concurrency counters, or mark as local-only/perf with generous tolerance and multiple warm-up runs; keep CI assertion on structural properties (0 subprocess calls, 50-model fixture count) rather than absolute ms. AC-037 fixed `now` is good — extend that pattern everywhere.\n5. Oracle quality: several ACs have weak/ambiguous oracles. AC-007 \"risk 为 critical 或 exhausted\" gives 2 valid values → pin to one or assert set membership explicitly with the threshold table; AC-008 \"给出 reason\" needs a reason enum; AC-035 example asks for 2/10, 1/5 — need to confirm Mtok unit (百万 token) and define the学习 formula for capacity from pct deltas (AC-038 \"带置信度\" needs the confidence formula + tolerance). AC-039 \"每个拒选都有原因\" needs a rejection-reason registry (tie to error-codes.snapshot). Make error/reason codes the single source of truth so AC-011 snapshot and AC-039/043/045 share it.\n6. Cross-platform matrix: win32 .cmd shim (AC-016), WSL UTF-16LE (AC-024), DPAPI/security/secret-tool (AC-020), adapters on 4 platforms (AC-029). CI likely single-platform. Strategy: split each into (a) pure unit on parsed fixtures (UTF-16LE decode, shim parse, quoting, buildCall arg arrays, gold fixtures) that run everywhere, and (b) platform-gated native spawn tests that SKIP with explicit reason. Require a skip manifest so AC-023/AC-024 \"跳过并记录原因\" is machine-checkable, not just a console message. Never let a skip count as pass for release (AC-055).\n7. Contract tests as first-class: contracts/examples + error-codes.snapshot.json must be generated/frozen in T-006 before downstream ACs (AC-041/043/045) depend on them; add a \"no silent field ignore\" test (AC-010's W_FIELD_IGNORED) and a recursive key/value scanner (AC-043) that must also scan nested values, error messages, warnings, and rejected[] — define the forbidden vocabulary list explicitly (cli/provider/vendor/model id/price/quota/forecast/direct command) and add a canary test that the scanner itself catches a deliberate leak (meta-test).\n8. Incremental/cumulative harnesses: secret-leak (AC-019) is built across T-009 → T-019 → T-020; sentinel helper must live in one shared helper with a single recursive state_dir byte-scan, and each milestone must re-run the FULL flow, not just the new stage. Same for check-docs (AC-053) and smoke report (AC-055).\n9. Rework risk M1→M4: T-004 introduces normalizeQuota/quota.mjs, T-017 rewrites/extends quota.mjs, forecast.mjs, and adds forecast/v1 fields; T-005 introduces errors.mjs初版, T-006 replaces with registry + snapshot. Strategy: write tests against the CONTRACT (contracts/examples, error-codes.snapshot) not against internal module shapes, so M1 tests survive M4 rework. Freeze the v1 contract surface in T-006 and only ADD fields thereafter (design already says forecast/v1 只加字段). Require a \"contract freeze\" gate: any rename/removal must update snapshot + fail AC-011.\n10. Flaky/concurrency tests: AC-013 (20 processes × 50 lines = 1000), AC-042 (50 concurrent selects), AC-017. Need: crash-injection hook (atomic write with a deliberate fail-before-rename), file lock with wx + stale reclaim with injectable clock, and assertions on invariants (no interleaving = every line parses; reserved ≤ remaining) rather than timing. Define concurrency test as bounded retries with a deterministic barrier, not sleeps.\n11. Packaging/CI: no lockfile, no CI config, no lint tooling, no scripts dir. AC-001 requires Node 20 AND Node 22; AC-002 requires pwsh. Need a CI matrix + pwsh availability confirmation. check-unused (AC-009) has no linter to build on — either add a devDependency (conflicts with \"zero deps\") or define a narrow, documented checker (e.g., ESLint via npx with pinned version, or a scoped AST scan) with a self-test that detects a deliberately-unused import. Zero-dependency constraint needs an explicit decision.\n12. Test-level ↔ directory consistency: AC levels vs task test_levels vs directories. AC-055 levels [\"smoke\",\"unit\"] but no test/smoke dir; smoke is a script run via CLIWORKER_SMOKE=1. AC-043 [\"contract\"] but T-018 test_levels includes contract + others. Define the canonical mapping: test/{unit,integration,contract,e2e}/ and smoke as script-only with a report-format unit test; run-tests.mjs must discover only `**/*.test.mjs` EXCLUDING fixtures/helpers, and check-test-discovery must compare the count to the actual executed files (AC-001 \"执行数与文件数一致\"). Need a strict exclude list for test/fixtures (fakecli.mjs etc.) to avoid counting non-test files.\n13. AC-055 real-machine smoke: depends on user's real config + credentials + DSH host; cannot be CI. Strategy: gate strictly behind CLIWORKER_SMOKE=1, make each step pass/skip-with-reason, fail blocks release, report redacted (reuse AC-019 scanner). Add a unit test for the report schema/redaction (already T-024) plus a dry-run mode on fixtures so the pipeline is exercised in CI without real CLIs.\n14. Coverage of design's own claims: fix the doc inaccuracies found (null TypeError mechanism; .gitignore literal vs glob; \"forecast 3 times\" = 3 call sites not 3 invocations; wrapped run --lease is a v2 target, not current baseline). These matter because AC-006/AC-005/AC-009 oracles reference them.\n\nBlockers — I should pick genuine blocking issues that must be resolved. Let me define them with id, status, text. status only open/resolved. Since it's a review, most will be \"open\" (things to resolve). Maybe I can include a couple \"resolved\" if the design already handles them — but a blocker that's resolved is arguably not a blocker. The user said \"没有阻塞时 blockers 为空数组\" and status can be open or resolved. I think I'll list open blockers (things that block testability/acceptance) and maybe mark one or two as resolved where the design already provides the mechanism — actually that's a good use of \"resolved\": e.g., \"需要 CI 双 Node 版本\" — not resolved. Hmm. I think the cleanest is to list only open blockers, which are genuine issues requiring a decision before implementation. But the schema allows \"resolved\" — perhaps to let the architect acknowledge a blocker that has already been addressed in the design. I'll include a couple resolved ones to show I checked (e.g., \"确定性预测需固定 now\" — design already says 输入固定的 now → resolved). That demonstrates thoroughness. But careful: a \"blocker\" marked resolved is odd. I'll frame them as \"曾被视为阻塞，设计已解决\" — acceptable. Actually, I think it's safer and more useful to make blockers a list of open issues only, with maybe 1-2 resolved. Let me include a small number of resolved to show the design addressed some testability concerns (that's the \"confirmed a non-obvious approach worked\" style). Hmm, but the field is \"blockers\" — a resolved item in a blockers list is contradictory unless framed as \"tracked and cleared\". I'll include 2 resolved entries explicitly labeled as such, which is useful for the orchestrator to know these were considered and cleared.\n\nActually, re-reading: `{\"id\":\"TB-1\",\"status\":\"open\",\"text\":\"阻塞说明\"}` — the example itself uses status \"open\". \"没有阻塞时 blockers 为空数组。status 只能是 open 或 resolved。\" So resolved is allowed. I think including resolved entries is fine and shows the review considered and cleared certain risks. But to keep it focused, I'll make most open and a couple resolved. Let me think about which are legitimately cleared by the design:\n- \"预测不确定性\" — design fixes with 固定 now + 不编数 + unknown → resolved.\n- \"探测消耗额度污染账本\" — design: 探测消耗以 kind=probe 记账、默认只手动触发 → resolved.\n- \"契约改名导致下游 AC 失效\" — design says 契约名不变、只加字段 → partially resolved but still needs snapshot freeze → I'd keep open with the remaining gap.\n- \"假 handle\" — design says 不返回假 handle 三条硬约束 → resolved (AC-030/041).\n\nHmm, I'll include maybe 3 resolved. Actually let me keep blockers focused on OPEN items primarily, since \"阻塞说明\" implies things blocking. I'll add a few resolved to demonstrate the design cleared them. Let's do ~8-10 open and 3 resolved. That's a thorough architect review.\n\nLet me carefully define open blockers with concrete grounding:\n\nTB-1 (open): DI seams — the single biggest cross-cutting blocker. Currently cli.mjs auto-runs main() on import and calls process.exit; availability.mjs imports spawnSync directly; no injectable exec/fs/clock (only forecast.mjs now is injectable). AC-009 (forecast counter), AC-018 (exec probe asserting 0 subprocess), AC-026 (fs access probe), AC-019 (sentinel argv/env capture), AC-046 (pseudo ctx/webServer), AC-022 (fake CLI) all require seams. Must be specified as a first-class contract (e.g., createContext injected through all modules; import-safe entrypoints) in M2 before those ACs can be written; otherwise tests must use brittle module mocking/monkeypatching. Also AC-046: apply() swallows registration errors in try/catch (console.error only) → a pseudo-ctx test can pass vacuously. Need apply() to surface/return registration results and a documented host stub.\n\nTB-2 (open): Weak/ambiguous oracles. AC-007 allows \"critical 或 exhausted\" (two outcomes) → pin one via threshold table or assert membership with explicit thresholds. AC-008 \"给出 reason\" needs a reason enum. AC-038 \"带置信度\" lacks the confidence formula and tolerance for capacity-from-pct learning. AC-035 must confirm Mtok = 百万 token and define the weighted sum formula precisely (design gives 剩余 = cap×(1−used), but AC-035 also wants 来自账本按 tokens/容量加权累加 — need the exact aggregation and rounding). AC-039 \"每个拒选都有原因\" needs a rejection-reason registry. Without these, tests will encode guesses and the design can drift.\n\nTB-3 (open): Timing/concurrency thresholds are CI-flaky. AC-017 (总耗时 < N/4+1 s), AC-018 (p95 < 300ms on 50-model fixture), AC-042 (50 concurrent), AC-048 health. Use injectable clock + logical concurrency counters/barriers; assert structural invariants (0 exec calls, reserved ≤ remaining, 1000 lines all parse) as the CI gate; move absolute ms/s thresholds to a local perf job with warm-up + generous tolerance + explicit machine pin, or drop them from gating. Also no CI config exists — who runs the matrix?\n\nTB-4 (open): Tooling/environment gaps: no lockfile, no scripts/, no CI config, no lint tooling, zero dependencies. AC-001 needs Node 20 AND Node 22 → need a CI matrix. AC-002 assumes `pwsh` — not verifiable here and not guaranteed on the runner; need to confirm or provide a fallback (e.g., a .ps1 invoked via powershell.exe on Windows, or a JS-equivalent check). AC-009 check-unused must report \"0 未使用导入和顶层函数\" with no existing linter — need to decide: add a pinned devDependency (breaks zero-dep posture) or write a narrow AST checker with a self-test that detects a deliberately unused import. Also `check-test-discovery` (AC-001) needs a strict exclude list for test/fixtures/ and test/helpers/ so non-test .mjs files aren't counted.\n\nTB-5 (open): Cross-platform tests can't run natively on a single CI OS. AC-016 (win32 .cmd shim + Node 20 CVE-2024-27980 direct-spawn rejection), AC-024 (WSL UTF-16LE + wsl.exe), AC-020 (DPAPI/security/secret-tool backends), AC-029 (adapters on 4 platforms). Strategy: split into pure unit tests on parsed fixtures (decode, shim-parse, quote, buildCall goldens) that run everywhere, plus platform-gated native spawn tests that skip with a machine-checkable skip manifest (AC-023/024 already say \"跳过并记录原因\" but that must be a structured record, not console text). Critical: a skip must NEVER count as a pass for AC-055 release gate. Need an explicit policy for which platform is the CI baseline.\n\nTB-6 (open): Contract freeze / M1→M4 rework risk. T-004 creates lib/quota.mjs + forecast path; T-017 rewrites quota.mjs/forecast.mjs and adds forecast/v1 fields. T-005 creates errors.mjs初版; T-006 replaces it with registry + error-codes.snapshot.json. Meanwhile AC-011/041/043/045 depend on the registry/snapshot from T-006. Tests written in M1 against internal shapes will break in M4. Require: freeze contracts/examples + error-codes.snapshot.json in T-006 as the single source of truth, have ALL downstream ACs assert against that frozen surface (only additive field changes allowed), and make AC-011's snapshot the gate for any rename/removal. Also need a contract-freeze check that fails when a code is deleted/renamed without a snapshot bump.\n\nTB-7 (open): Doc/baseline inaccuracies that poison AC oracles. Grounded: (a) null-config TypeError comes from `${raw.schema}` in the thrown literal, not `raw.schema &&` (which short-circuits) — AC-006's fix/test must target the real line; (b) .gitignore currently has literal `config/cliworker.local.json` and `usage.jsonl`, NOT globs `config/*.local.json` / `*.jsonl`, and no `state/` — AC-005's `git check-ignore` oracle must be written against the glob behavior, and the design's §1 claim is wrong; (c) \"forecast 调用 3 次\" = 3 call sites, but the sort comparator invokes it ~2×/comparison, so AC-009 \"每个候选 forecast 只计算一次\" needs per-model memoization, not just removing a call site — the injected counter must count invocations, not call sites; (d) there is NO current `run --lease`/`resolve`/wrapped call — that's a v2 target; T-019's runner tests are greenfield, not regression, so they need fresh goldens (AC-044/045) rather than a diff against current behavior. Need the design doc corrected before ACs are finalized.\n\nTB-8 (open): Incremental/cumulative harness ownership. AC-019 sentinel-token leak test is built across T-009 → T-019 → T-020 and must scan stdout, stderr, ALL state_dir files, audit.jsonl, and HTTP responses, plus assert env-only injection and absence from argv. Without one shared, owned helper, each stage will implement a partial scanner and later stages won't re-run the full flow; risk of a false pass where a leak appears only in the HTTP path. Same for