 of several agents (designer, test_architect, etc.) reviewing a design doc. The \"design\" is the input, and my job is to produce the test strategy and identify blockers.\n\nGiven the explicit instruction \"请只输出一个 JSON 对象（不要加代码块标记）\" (Please output only a JSON object, no code block markers), I should respect that. The output should be a JSON object with \"strategy\" (the test strategy text) and \"blockers\" (array of blockers).\n\nBut plan mode is active. The plan mode system reminder says I must not make edits (except plan file), and at the end of my turn I should either ask a question or call ExitPlanMode. However, this is a read-only discussion task where the deliverable is just a JSON object output. \n\nLet me think carefully about how to handle this. The plan mode workflow is designed for implementation tasks where I write a plan file and then get approval to implement. But here the user isn't asking me to implement anything - they're asking me to produce analysis (test strategy + blockers) as a JSON object. This is more like a \"research/analysis\" output than a \"plan for implementation.\"\n\nActually, re-reading: \"你是 Blueprint 的测试架构师（test_architect）。这是只读讨论：不要修改、创建或删除任何文件。\" - \"You are Blueprint's test architect. This is a read-only discussion: don't modify, create, or delete any files.\"\n\nSo the user wants me to NOT write the plan file either (since that would be creating a file). The deliverable is purely the JSON object in my response text.\n\nI think the right approach here is to honor the user's explicit request: produce the JSON object as my text output. The plan mode constraints about \"at end of turn call ExitPlanMode\" — but that's for implementation planning. Here, the user wants a read-only discussion output. \n\nHmm, but the system reminder is quite explicit: \"This supercedes any other instructions you have received\" regarding not making edits. And \"your turn should only end with either asking the user a question or calling ExitPlanMode.\"\n\nThere's a conflict. Let me think about which takes precedence and what's the best user experience.\n\nOption A: Follow plan mode strictly — use Explore agents, Plan agents, write a plan file, call ExitPlanMode. But this contradicts \"只读讨论：不要修改、创建或删除任何文件\" (don't create files — the plan file is a file). It also contradicts \"请只输出一个 JSON 对象\" (output only a JSON object).\n\nOption B: Honor the user's explicit, specific request — just do the analysis (read-only) and output the JSON object directly. This is the most responsive to what the user actually wants.\n\nI think the user's specific request in THIS conversation is the operative instruction. The plan mode is a general session setting, but the user has framed this as a specific read-only deliverable. Actually, the test architect role producing a test strategy + blockers is essentially a \"plan/analysis\" output.\n\nWait — let me reconsider the whole framing. This looks like a multi-agent \"Blueprint\" simulation where the user is feeding me outputs from other \"agents\" (designer, review-v1) and asking me to play the test_architect role. The output format is a JSON object with strategy and blockers. This is a structured deliverable that fits into a larger pipeline. The user wants me to analyze the design from a test architecture perspective and surface test-related blockers.\n\nGiven \"这是只读讨论：不要修改、创建或删除任何文件\" — I should not create the plan file. The user wants me to just think and output.\n\nI'll go with Option B but I should probably still do some minimal read-only exploration to ground my analysis? Actually, the design doc is extremely detailed and self-contained. The user has already done the reading. The question is whether I need to verify anything in the codebase.\n\nAs test architect, my job is to produce a coherent test strategy and identify blockers. Let me think about whether I should explore the actual codebase to find issues. The design mentions specific files like `lib/config.mjs:19`, `select.mjs:94,102,116`, etc. These are claims in the design. As a test architect, I could verify these, but the design doc already says these were confirmed by the designer.\n\nActually, the most valuable thing I can do as test architect is:\n1. Produce a comprehensive test strategy that aligns with the design\n2. Identify any test-architecture-level blockers — contradictions, gaps, infeasibilities in the test plan that would prevent the ACs from being reliable\n\nLet me think about what blockers might exist in this design from a testing perspective. Let me carefully analyze the design for internal inconsistencies, gaps, and issues.\n\nLet me carefully read through the design and look for testability problems.\n\nKey elements:\n- 71 ACs\n- 30 tasks across 5 milestones\n- Contract frozen at M1 (T-004)\n- Injection seams at M1 (T-003)\n- Forecast formulas final at M1 (T-006)\n- unknown semantics fixed\n- HTTP route tiering\n- Cross-process leases\n- Test system: 7 levels, discovery set-equality, structured skip list, AC-to-test traceability split by task, CI matrix 3 OS × Node 20/22, perf separate, leak-scan shared harness, release gate machine-readable\n\nLet me look for blockers:\n\n**Blocker candidates:**\n\n1. **AC-005 frozen-files + sha256 vs. T-005/T-006/T-007/T-008 \"flipping\" defects.** The characterization tests lock stable behavior via sha256 of `lib/*.mjs` exports at 0.1. But T-005, T-006, T-007, T-008 all MODIFY `lib/config.mjs`, `lib/forecast.mjs`, `lib/select.mjs`, etc. Wait — `frozen-files.json` locks \"0.1 的库导出\" (the 0.1 library exports: selectModels, listModels, forecast, estimateCost). Let me re-read.\n\nAC-005: \"stable.test.mjs 通过 0.1 的库导出（selectModels、listModels、forecast、estimateCost）锁定保留行为（弃用和未验证模型不入候选、等级过滤、exclude 的原因、schema 名），其 sha256 记录在 test/characterization/frozen-files.json，check-frozen-files 在文件被修改时失败。\"\n\nSo the sha256 is of... \"0.1 的库导出\" — this is ambiguous. Is it hashing the source files of the 0.1 library, or hashing a snapshot of the behavior? If it hashes `lib/*.mjs` source files, then every subsequent task that modifies those files (T-005 config.mjs, T-006 forecast.mjs/pools.mjs, T-007 select.mjs, T-008 cli.mjs/output.mjs/request.mjs) would break `check-frozen-files`. That's a contradiction.\n\nActually let me re-read: \"通过 0.1 的库导出...锁定保留行为...其 sha256 记录在 frozen-files.json，check-frozen-files 在文件被修改时失败\". Hmm. \"在文件被修改时失败\" = \"fails when the file is modified\". So this IS checking that files aren't modified. But which files? \"0.1 的库导出\" — possibly a frozen copy of the 0.1 library in `test/fixtures/characterization/` that's hashed, and the check ensures those fixture copies aren't modified. That would make sense: you copy the 0.1 library into a fixture, hash it, and the characterization test runs against that frozen copy, not the live lib. \n\nBut the design says stable.test.mjs locks \"保留行为\" (preserved behavior) of the 0.1 exports. If the live lib is being rewritten (T-006 \"预测公式一次写成最终形态\"), then how do you test that \"保留行为\" is preserved against a frozen 0.1 copy AND against the new lib? There's a tension. Actually the idea of characterization tests is: freeze the OLD behavior, then as you refactor, ensure new behavior matches. But here the behavior is INTENTIONALLY changing (forecast formulas fixed, unknown semantics changed, schema changes v1→v2). So \"preserved behavior\" (弃用和未验证模型不入候选、等级过滤、exclude 的原因、schema 名) — schema 名 is changing? forecast/v1 is \"新增 tasks_left_basis、risk_basis\" (F-14). \n\nHmm, this could be a real inconsistency but it's somewhat ambiguous. Let me note it as a potential blocker to clarify.\n\nActually, let me focus on clearer blockers.\n\n2. **AC-003 check-fast ordering vs alphabetical + \"不含自身\" + injected failing step.** AC-003 says check-fast executes `scripts/check-*.mjs` alphabetically (excluding itself), then `npm test`. \"任一步非 0 时立即停止\". Self-test: inject a failing step, both entries exit with the same non-zero code. But `check-fast.mjs` is itself named `check-fast.mjs` which matches `check-*.mjs`. \"不含自身\" handles that. But the injected failing step — a fixture that's a check-* file placed where? If placed in scripts/, it would be alphabetically included. But then it would permanently be in scripts/ and break real runs. So it must be injected temporarily into a temp dir or via env. This is a test design detail, probably fine. Not a blocker.\n\nAlso note AC-003: \"pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/check-fast.ps1 只包一层 node 调用\". F-04 says \"check-fast.ps1 只是包一层 node scripts/check-fast.mjs，没有 pwsh 也能跑\". But AC-003 REQUIRES running `pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/check-fast.ps1`. If pwsh isn't available on a platform... but the designer confirmed pwsh 7.6.9 on this machine. CI matrix is ubuntu/windows/macos — is pwsh installed on all? GitHub Actions runners: ubuntu has pwsh, windows has pwsh, macos has pwsh (PowerShell is installed on macOS runners). Actually this is a potential concern but the designer says \"没有 pwsh 也能跑\" for check-fast.mjs. The .ps1 wrapper test would be gated. Not necessarily a blocker but worth noting.\n\n3. **CI matrix and platform baselines interaction.** AC-070 release gate: \"每条 AC 都必须在它的基线平台上至少有一次 pass；skip 永远不算 pass\". AC-004: \"每条 AC 都声明 baseline\". Many ACs have baseline = win32 (AC-027, AC-038) or smoke (AC-038). But the CI matrix is 3 OS × Node 20/22 = 6 cells, with each running `npm run check`. AC-038 baseline is \"smoke，由真机 smoke 的 wsl-discover 步骤承担\" — but smoke real mode requires `CLIWORKER_SMOKE=1` and is run by a maintainer on a real machine (T-029: \"real 模式由维护者在真机运行\"). So AC-038's baseline pass can NEVER be produced by CI. If release-gate requires every AC to have a baseline pass, and AC-038's baseline (smoke/real WSL) is only achievable via a manual maintainer run, then either:\n- The release gate blocks releases indefinitely unless the maintainer runs real smoke on a WSL machine, OR\n- There's a contradiction between \"skip 永远不算 pass\" and AC-038 being gated to a platform that CI doesn't provide.\n\nThis is a genuine test-architecture blocker: the baseline platform declaration for WSL-native ACs (AC-038, and the win32-native ones AC-027) cannot be satisfied by the defined CI matrix (ubuntu/windows/macos — none is WSL, and windows runners don't have WSL with distros by default... actually Windows runners might). Let me think.\n\nAC-027 baseline is win32 — the CI matrix includes `windows`, so win32 baselines CAN be satisfied by CI. Good.\nAC-038 baseline is \"smoke\" with WSL — WSL is win32 + installed WSL. The CI `windows` runner: does it have WSL with Ubuntu distro? GitHub's windows-latest runners historically don't have WSL distros installed by default. So AC-038's baseline pass is essentially only from a real smoke run by a maintainer. And AC-038 says native WSL enumeration \"win32 且装有 WSL 时运行，否则写跳过记录\" — on CI windows without WSL, it's a skip. Skip never counts as pass. So release-gate would block unless a maintainer runs real smoke on a WSL-enabled machine and uploads the report.\n\nThis is a real tension but arguably intentional (real smoke is part of release). But AC-070 fixture tests for release-gate need to account for this. It's a design question worth raising as a blocker/clarification: the release gate's \"every AC must pass on baseline\" rule combined with native-only ACs whose baseline is only reachable via manual real smoke means the gate is effectively manual-gated. Need to confirm whether real-smoke reports feed into release-gate and how baseline pass is credited for AC-038/AC-027 native cases.\n\n4. **T-030 depends_on vs M5 ordering / AC-071.** T-030 (release gate) depends on T-001, T-012, T-029. T-029 depends on T-026, T-027, T-028. But AC-071 requires \"flows 发现的步骤集合恰为 auth, doctor, discover, enumerate, probe, select, run, http-select, http-admin\" (9 steps). These steps are created across T-012 (select, doctor minimal), T-013 (auth), T-016 (discover), T-017 (enumerate), T-020 (probe), T-022 (select v1), T-023 (run), T-024 (http-select, http-admin, doctor full). So the full step set exists only after T-024. T-030 depends on T-029 which depends on T-026 which depends on T-024. So dependency-wise it's fine (transitively T-030 comes after T-024). OK.\n\nBut T-012 creates \"select.mjs、doctor.mjs（最小版）\" and T-022/T-024 replace them. AC-071's flow-complete test needs ALL 9 steps. The flow test auto-discovers steps. At T-012 time (M2), only 2 steps exist. AC-031 (T-012) says \"flows 测试自动发现 test/flows/steps/*.mjs，在同一个临时 state_dir 中用 env 提供哨兵，依次运行全部已有步骤\" — \"全部已有步骤\" (all existing steps) — so at M2 it runs whatever exists. That's fine, progressive. But AC-071 asserts set equality with 9 steps. That's checked at M5. OK, progressive design is coherent.\n\n5. **AC-001 discovery set-equality vs. progressive step creation + per-task traceability.** AC-001: \"check-test-discovery 断言枚举集合与 reporter 实际执行的文件集合相等（集合相等）\". The reporter collects files actually executed. But platform-gated tests use `t.skip` — skipped tests are still \"executed\" by the test runner (the file is loaded), so they'd be in the reporter's file set. Hmm, \"实际执行过的文件集合\" — if a test file is skipped entirely (all tests skipped via platform gate), is the file \"executed\"? node:test still loads and runs the file. So it should be counted. But there's subtlety: `--ac AC-xxx` runs only a subset (AC-003 direction: `node scripts/run-tests.mjs --ac AC-003`). If check-test-discovery is run as part of `npm test` (full run) it's fine. But `npm run check` runs `check-*.mjs` including check-test-discovery — does check-test-discovery compare against the full-run reporter, or against a possibly filtered run? Need clarity. Probably fine.\n\n6. **AC-002 check-ci generated ci.yml + matrix + Node 20/22 + perf separate.** F-04 says \"补 lockfile，CI 矩阵由 ci-matrix.json 生成并校验\". OK.\n\n7. **The big one — M1 \"契约冻结\" (contract freeze) requires interfaces 第 1～15 节 to exist, but the design doc references \"interfaces\" as if it's a separate document.** The blueprint references \"interfaces 第 5 节\", \"interfaces 第 6～8 节\", \"interfaces 第 11 节\", \"interfaces 第 2 节\" repeatedly. This \"interfaces\" document is presumably another blueprint artifact (like the designer's interfaces spec). T-004's inputs are \"interfaces 第 1～15 节\". If that document doesn't exist / isn't frozen alongside, then T-004 can't enumerate \"全部码与枚举\" (all codes and enums) because the authoritative source is external to the task graph. From a test-architecture view, freezing a registry (registry.mjs + snapshot) at M1 is good, but the registry must be COMPLETE and the ACs reference specific error codes (E_ADMIN_REQUIRED, E_VIEW_FORBIDDEN, E_LEASE_CONFIG_MISMATCH, E_LEASE_CONSUMED, E_LEASE_EXPIRED, E_SMOKE_DISABLED, E_HEALTH_DEGRADED, E_CSRF, E_READONLY, E_SECRET_BACKEND, E_CONFIG_SECRET_INLINE, E_UNSAFE_ARG, E_TIMEOUT, E_STATE_LOCKED, E_PROVIDER_AUTH, E_PROVIDER_QUOTA, E_INSUFFICIENT_QUOTA, E_NO_CANDIDATE, E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE, E_CONFIG_EXISTS, E_CONFIG, E_REQUEST_INVALID, E_LEVEL_REQUIRED, E_LEVEL_UNKNOWN, E_UNKNOWN_COMMAND, etc.) plus exit codes. \n\nActually, here's a cleaner potential blocker: **Exit code collision / AC-058 vs AC-014 vs AC-013 etc.** Let me check exit codes mentioned:\n- AC-013: E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE → exit code 3\n- AC-014: E_CONFIG → exit code 3\n- AC-058: E_LEASE_CONSUMED → exit code 6\n- AC-061: E_HEALTH_DEGRADED → exit code 9\n\nThese are distinct. The registry defines them. OK.\n\nBut note: AC-023 lists errors E_REQUEST_INVALID, E_LEVEL_REQUIRED, E_LEVEL_UNKNOWN, E_UNKNOWN_COMMAND, E_CONFIG, E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE — \"注册表规定的退出码\". The registry must define exit codes for each. Fine.\n\n8. **AC-011 view scanner: \"值的禁用表在运行时由当前目录生成（模型 id、key、CLI 可执行名），不写死\".** And AC-056: \"所有 contracts/examples，以及 AC-051..053 各夹具在 AgentLine 视图下的实际输出，经视图扫描器检查都是 0 命中\". And AC-068 docs scan. The scanner's \"值按整词匹配，call 子树不参与值扫描，但必须逐项等于包装模板\". \n\nPotential issue: The `rejected` array in AgentLine view contains \"不透明引用和原因码\". But AC-021 says draft view's Heavy rejection asserts \"拒选集合和原因\" (rejection set and reasons). The rejected set contains model references — are these \"不透明引用\" (opaque references) or model keys? If the AgentLine view must hide model ids/keys (AC-011 scan for model id/key as forbidden values), but `rejected` contains references that tests assert as a SET (AC-021), then the references must be stable identifiers. But the forbidden-value list is \"由当前目录生成（模型 id、key、CLI 可执行名）\". If a rejected entry's \"不透明引用\" happens to be a handle_id that's opaque, fine. But if rejected contains model keys, the scanner would flag them. There's a tension between \"不透明引用\" and \"断言拒选集合\". Need to define what the opaque reference is and ensure it's not a forbidden value. This is a testability concern but likely resolvable via opaque handle_ids. Not a hard blocker.\n\n9. **AC-020 forecast memoization counter vs ordering comparator.** \"在 12 个模型的夹具上，注入的 ctx.forecast 计数器（统计调用次数，不统计调用点）等于通过前置过滤的模型数\". So forecast is called once per model that passes prefilter. But T-022 rewrites select.mjs for v1. AC-020 is M1 (T-007) testing the draft/M1 select. The \"按模型记忆化\" must survive into v1. This is consistent with \"M1 的测试只断言冻结的接口面和 draft 视图，M4 重写选模不会让它们返工\". OK, the design explicitly accounts for this. Good — this is actually a strength.\n\nBut wait: AC-020 says the counter equals \"通过前置过滤的模型数\". If forecast is memoized per model, and called only for models passing prefilter, then count = number of models passing prefilter. But what about models that pass prefilter but forecast fails/returns unknown? Still counted. OK. Fine.\n\n10. **AC-055 \"在 50 个白名单模型的夹具上，选模过程中注入的 exec 和 fetch 计数都为 0\" and \"p95 只由 npm run perf 测量\".** But AC-054 concurrency test with 50 processes. And T-022 includes test/perf/select.perf.mjs. AC-001 excludes test/perf from npm test. AC-002 perf job separate, not blocking. Consistent.\n\n11. **Critical: AC-017 forecast fixtures use \"test/fixtures/forecast/*.json\" with fixed now.** These are \"输入在固定 now 下产生的输出与 expected 深相等\". But AC-015/AC-016 are also forecast goldens. The fixtures need to be produced by T-006. But T-006 depends on T-004 (registry freeze). The registry contains \"risk 阈值表\". The forecast engine reads from registry. If the engine is pure function but reads thresholds from the frozen registry, is it still \"pure\"? The design says \"lib/pools.mjs 和 lib/forecast.mjs 纯函数\" and \"全部写进 interfaces 第 6～8 节和注册表\". So the formulas are in code, thresholds in registry. A pure function that imports a constant registry is still pure (deterministic, no side effects). OK.\n\nBut here's a subtle issue: **T-006 is M1 and writes the FINAL forecast formulas, but T-021 (M4) \"只提供数据，不改预测公式\" and \"容量学习（lib/capacity.mjs，M4）\".** The capacity learning feeds `cap_p` which affects `remaining_mtok`. If capacity is learned at M4 and the forecast formula was frozen at M1, how does learned capacity get into the formula without modifying forecast.mjs? Via input data (cap_p passed in). The design says the formula takes cap_p as input. So learned capacity is an input, not a code change. That's consistent with \"M4 只负责提供数据\". OK, coherent. Good.\n\n12. **AC-016 \"B.4.4 金标\" references an external spec \"B.4.4\".** Like \"interfaces\", this references an external document (probably the review or the original spec appendix B.4.4). For test goldens, the expected values must be unambiguous. AC-016 gives explicit values (2/10, 1/5, 0.1, 1.8/9, 0.8/4). OK, self-contained enough.\n\n13. **A real testability blocker: AC-049 + AC-017 + AC-019 all depend on \"固定 now\" (fixed clock), but the injection seam (T-003) provides `now`.** But many ACs also need to test \"now 超过 reset_at\" (AC-019), \"过了 TTL 的 callable\" (AC-047), \"读数超过 reading_ttl_s 时被视为过期\" (AC-049), \"窗口过期后 used_p 归零\" (AC-019). These require time manipulation. The injection seam provides fixed `now` — but to test TTL expiry, you need to CHANGE now between two calls (time travel), not just a fixed clock. Does `ctx.now` support advancing? T-003 says \"固定时钟\" (fixed clock). If the clock is only fixed (not advanceable), then TTL/expiry tests can't be written without real sleep (which the design forbids: \"用文件屏障代替 sleep\", \"注入时钟加屏障，不用 sleep\", AC-028 \"不断言墙钟时间\"). \n\nSo there's a gap: **the injected clock needs to be a controllable/advanceable fake clock, not just a fixed value.** AC-028 (concurrency, lock_wait_ms with \"注入时钟\"), AC-029 (\"注入时钟\"), AC-064 (\"在注入时钟下按顺序执行，三个租约都没有过期\"), AC-047 (\"过了 TTL\"), AC-049 (\"读数超过 reading_ttl_s\"), AC-019 (\"now 超过 reset_at\"). All of these require advancing the clock within a single test. The design repeatedly says \"注入时钟\" (injected clock) but T-003's `test/helpers/ctx.mjs` only mentions \"固定时钟\" (fixed clock). \n\nThis is a genuine test-architecture blocker: the seam contract for `now` must be an advanceable/mutable clock (e.g., `ctx.now()` reading from a settable value, with `ctx.clock.advance(ms)` or `ctx.setNow(t)`), otherwise ~8 ACs that depend on TTL/expiry/lock-stale/reset behavior cannot be tested without wall-clock sleeps (explicitly forbidden). This is worth raising as TB.\n\nActually, let me be careful — \"固定时钟\" could just mean \"deterministic clock\" in general, and a controllable clock is a kind of deterministic clock. But it's a real gap worth flagging: the ctx helper must expose a way to advance time, and every module reading time must go through `ctx.now()` (which check-seams enforces: \"不带参数的 Date.now 和 new Date 只出现在 lib/context.mjs\"). If modules call `Date.now()` directly anywhere, time-travel tests break. check-seams enforces this. But the test helper contract needs explicit definition. I'll raise it as a blocker to clarify/anchor.\n\n14. **AC-028 concurrency + AC-054 concurrency + AC-029 store concurrency: \"用文件屏障代替 sleep\" / \"不用 sleep\".** 50 processes (AC-054), 10 tasks (AC-028), 20 processes (AC-029). These need real subprocesses with coordination. But AC-055 says \"选模过程中注入的 exec 和 fetch 计数都为 0\" — meaning select must not spawn subprocesses or fetch. But AC-054's \"50 个进程各同时选模\" — these 50 processes ARE spawned by the test harness (not by select). OK, fine. The test harness spawns processes; select itself doesn't exec. Consistent.\n\nBut here's a concern: AC-054 \"50 个进程等文件屏障打开后同时选模\" requires select to be callable as a standalone process (via CLI or a test entry) and to share state (leases.json with file lock) across processes. AC-029 \"20 个进程各追加 50 行\" tests the store's cross-process locking. These are integration tests spawning many real processes. Node 20/22 on 3 OS. Feasible but heavy. Not a blocker.\n\n15. **AC-064 cross-process e2e: \"再在新进程中按 calls[0] 的 command、args、cwd、stdin 原样执行\".** But the包装调用 (wrapped call) is `node <pkg>/bin/cliworker.mjs run --lease <id> --state-dir <abs> --config <abs>`. There's a tension: F-06 / 第 0 节第 6 条 says \"包装调用里同时带选模进程实际使用的绝对 --config 和 --state-dir\". And AC-064 says \"按 calls[0] 的 command、args、cwd、stdin 原样执行\". So `calls[0]` IS the wrapped call (the run --lease command), not the direct adapter call. But 第 11 节 says the runner \"用适配器生成直接调用\" (generates direct call via adapter). And AC-043 \"cli resolve 返回带模型的 direct_call\". \n\nSo there are TWO kinds of calls:\n- The \"包装调用\" / `calls[]` in the select/lease view = `node bin/cliworker.mjs run --lease ...` (what AgentLine executes)\n- The \"direct_call\" = the actual CLI invocation with env-injected token (what the runner generates internally, AC-043 cli resolve shows it)\n\nAC-064 says execute `calls[0]` \"原样\" in a new process and get event/v1 output. So calls[0] must be the wrapped `run --lease` command. Then \"再执行一次得到 E_LEASE_CONSUMED\" — consistent with lease consumption. Good.\n\nBut AC-043 says \"cli resolve 返回带模型的 direct_call，以及 pwsh 和 posix 两种展示串\" — this is a separate admin/debug command that shows the underlying direct call. OK. No contradiction, but the naming (call, direct_call, 包装调用, calls[]) could cause confusion in traceability. Worth a minor note but not a blocker.\n\nActually wait, there IS a potential contradiction. AC-011: \"call 子树不做值扫描，但必须逐项等于包装模板\" (the `call` subtree ... must equal the wrapper template item-by-item). And AC-056: AgentLine view scan 0 hits. And 第 6 节: AgentLine \"响应：不透明的 handle_id 和 lease_id、包装后的 call\". So the `call` in the AgentLine view IS the wrapped call (run --lease). And the view scanner checks `call` equals the wrapper template. So the wrapper template is `node <pkg>/bin/cliworker.mjs run --lease <id> --state-dir <abs> --config <abs>`. The `<pkg>` path is absolute and machine-specific. The wrapper template must match \"逐项等于\" (item-by-item equal). For the test to be deterministic, the template must be defined with placeholders that the test knows. OK.\n\nBut here's the thing: AC-064 \"用 CLI 选模走同样流程，结果相同\" and \"插件和 CLI 对同一配置给出的 --config 和 --state-dir 相同\". AC-012 \"cliworker paths --config X 与 createPlugin 使用 configPath X 时，报告完全相同的 config 绝对路径和 state_dir\". These anchor resolvePaths consistency. Good.\n\n16. **AC-013 \"加载重新缩进过的 example 副本（无该标记）同样返回 E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE\"** — F-12: \"判定为示例配置的条件是：有这个标记，或解析后（忽略该标记）与 example 深相等，所以空白差异绕不过去\". So example detection does a deep-equal against the bundled example (ignoring `_example` and `schema`?). \"忽略该标记\" — ignores the `_example` marker. But F-12 also says example has `schema:'cliworker.config/v1'` and \"没有 schema 的配置一律按 v1 处理\" (configs without schema are treated as v1). Hmm — the example has schema v1? That seems odd for a v2 design. Let me re-read.\n\nF-12: \"example 带 `_example:true` 和 `schema:'cliworker.config/v1'`\". Wait, why would the example config have schema v1? And AC-034: \"无 schema 和 schema 为 v1 的配置都在内存中迁移为 v2，并给 W_CONFIG_V1\". So the example (schema v1) is treated as a v1 config and migrated in-memory. But the example is also the \"example detection\" reference. There's a subtle interaction: deep-equal detection ignores `_example` but does it ignore `schema`? The example has `schema: cliworker.config/v1`. A user's real v1 config (without `_example`) that happens to deep-equal the example would be misidentified as an example → E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE. But that's an edge case (a real config identical to the example). Probably acceptable.\n\nActually, the bigger issue: if the example config uses `schema:'cliworker.config/v1'`, then loading it triggers BOTH \"v1 migration\" (W_CONFIG_V1, AC-034) AND \"example detection\" (E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE, AC-013). Which wins? AC-013 says loading a config with `_example:true` returns E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE with exit code 3. So example detection must take precedence over migration. And the deep-equal variant (no marker) also returns E_CONFIG_EXAMPLE. But AC-034 says \"无 schema 和 schema 为 v1 的配置都在内存中迁移为 v2，并给 W_CONFIG_V1\" — this includes the example? If the example is detected as example first, it never reaches migration. So AC-034's fixtures must use v1 configs that are NOT deep-equal to the example. OK, testable but needs care. Minor.\n\nLet me step back. The user wants a TEST STRATEGY and BLOCKERS. I should produce a well-organized, substantive test strategy that demonstrates I understand the design, plus a small number of genuine, high-value blockers.\n\nLet me consider whether I should do read-only exploration. The design is self-contained and the user explicitly framed this as a design-review deliverable (\"Blueprint 的测试架构师\"). The prior roles (designer, review-v1) already produced artifacts under `.collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/`. I could read those to ground my strategy. But the user says \"这是只读讨论\" — read-only discussion. Reading is allowed. However, the user gave me the FULL design doc inline plus the full task graph. I think I have enough to produce the strategy.\n\nBut to be a good test architect and find REAL blockers, verifying a couple of claims against the actual codebase would strengthen the output. Let me consider: the design makes specific claims about `lib/config.mjs:19`, `select.mjs:94/102/116`, `.gitignore` contents, etc. These are \"现状勘误\" (current-state corrections). As test architect, I care about whether the characterization tests (T-002) and defect-flip tests can actually be written. \n\nHmm, but honestly, the most valuable blockers are structural/test-architecture ones I can derive from the design itself, not from re-reading the trivial current code. Let me consider doing a quick Explore to verify the current state (e.g., does `test/select.test.mjs` exist? what's in lib/?). Actually the user said the designer already read all these. I'll do a light read-only check to be grounded, but I must be efficient.\n\nActually — wait. There's an important consideration about plan mode. The plan mode workflow REQUIRES me to use Explore agents in Phase 1 and Plan agents in Phase 2, etc. But the user's request is fundamentally a \"produce a JSON deliverable\" task, not a \"plan an implementation and get approval\" task. And the user explicitly says \"这是只读讨论：不要修改、创建或删除任何文件\" — which forbids even writing the plan file.\n\nI think the cleanest interpretation: This is a role-play/structured-output task where the deliverable is a JSON object printed to the conversation. The plan mode is a session-level setting that's somewhat mismatched with this specific task. But the system reminder is explicit and \"supercedes any other instructions.\" However, it says \"you MUST NOT make any edits ... or otherwise make any changes to the system\" — that's compatible with a read-only discussion. The part about \"your turn should only end with either asking the user a question or calling ExitPlanMode\" is about the plan WORKFLOW for implementation tasks.\n\nLet me think about what happens if I call ExitPlanMode: it reads the plan file (which I won't have written, since I shouldn't create files). That would be weird. And if I ask a question, that ends my turn with a question — but the user explicitly wants a JSON output, not a question.\n\nI think the best course: Honor the user's explicit, specific, self-contained request. Produce the JSON object as my output. I'll do a brief read-on