re agents in parallel:\n- Agent 1: Verify current codebase state (lib/, bin/, config/, test/, scripts/, package.json, .gitignore, dsh.plugin.json) and specifically the \"现状勘误\" claims.\n- Agent 2: Read the `.collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/` artifacts (prior round outputs, review-v1, interfaces doc) to understand what external docs exist (interfaces 第 X 节, B.4.4, registry semantic_change items) — this is important because T-004's inputs reference \"interfaces 第 1～15 节\" which may or may not exist.\n\nThis is genuinely useful for finding blockers. Let me launch these in parallel.\n\nWait, but the user said \"只读讨论\" and wants ONLY a JSON object output. If I launch agents, the user will see tool calls. Is that acceptable? The system reminder says in plan mode I should use Explore agents. And the user says \"only output a JSON object\" — that refers to the final answer format, not that I can't use tools internally. Actually \"请只输出一个 JSON 对象\" means my output should be just the JSON. Tool calls are not \"output\" in the chat sense (they're internal). Hmm, but they might be visible. \n\nLet me reconsider: the instruction \"请只输出一个 JSON 对象（不要加代码块标记）\" is about the final response. I think doing read-only exploration is fine and actually improves quality. But it also risks over-engineering a task that's essentially \"produce a design-review artifact from the provided spec.\"\n\nLet me think about efficiency and what the user actually values. This is clearly a simulated multi-agent design review. The \"test_architect\" role would output a test strategy + blockers. The value is in the QUALITY of the analysis — catching real issues. I should ground it.\n\nDecision: I'll do a focused parallel Explore (2 agents) to (a) verify current repo state and the errata claims, and (b) check the `.collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/` artifacts for the referenced external docs (interfaces, B.4.4, review-v1). Then I'll synthesize the test strategy + blockers and output the JSON. I will NOT create the