ust be an advanceable/mutable clock, not just a fixed value.** Many ACs (AC-019 reset, AC-028 lock_wait_ms, AC-029 lock_stale_ms/window expiry, AC-047 availability TTL, AC-049 reading_ttl_s staleness, AC-058 lease expiry, AC-064 3-lease deferred expiry \"在注入时钟下按顺序执行\") require advancing time within a single test process, while the design forbids wall-clock sleeps (\"用文件屏障代替 sleep\", \"注入时钟加屏障，不用 sleep\"). T-003 only specifies a \"固定时钟\" and `check-seams` only bans bare `Date.now`/`new Date` outside `lib/context.mjs`. Unless `test/helpers/ctx.mjs` exposes a settable/advanceable clock API AND every module consumes time strictly via `ctx.now()`, ~10 ACs are untestable. Need to pin the clock seam contract at M1.\n\n**TB-2: Release-gate \"every AC must pass on its baseline platform; skip never counts as pass\" is unsatisfiable for native-only ACs whose baseline is outside the CI matrix.** AC-027 baseline win32 (OK, windows runner exists), but AC-038 baseline is \"smoke / 真机 wsl-discover\" — WSL-with-distro is not on the ubuntu/windows/macos CI matrix and real smoke runs only under `CLIWORKER_SMOKE=1` by a maintainer (T-029). AC-070 blocks release when any AC has only skip on its baseline. So either the gate permanently blocks unless a maintainer manually runs real WSL smoke and feeds the report into release-gate (the report→gate data path is not defined in T-030's inputs/outputs), or AC-038/AC-027 must be exempted/re-baselined. Need to define how native/smoke baseline passes are credited and which ACs are exempt.\n\nHmm, actually AC-027 baseline win32 IS in the matrix. AC-038 is the problem. Also AC-038's `levels` is `[\"integration\"]` but baseline is \"smoke\" — inconsistent: the AC declares integration level but smoke baseline. And AC-069 (smoke dry-run) uses fake-cli, no WSL. So real WSL enumeration has no CI-produced pass. Good blocker.\n\n**TB-3: \"interfaces\" / \"B.4.4\" are referenced as the authoritative source for the frozen registry but are external to the task graph.** T-004's inputs are \"interfaces 第 1～15 节\", AC-015/016/043 reference \"interfaces 第 X 节\" and \"B.4.4 金标\", F-03 says formulas go \"写进 interfaces 第 6～8 节和注册表\". The registry (`registry.mjs` + `registry.snapshot.json`) is frozen at M1 and is the single source of truth for codes/enums/thresholds. If the interfaces spec is not itself versioned/frozen and merged into `contracts/` before T-004, the freeze is against a moving/unavailable document, and AC-010's snapshot comparison has no stable oracle. Need to confirm the interfaces/B.4.4 spec is a committed, frozen artifact in `contracts/` (or absorbed into registry) before T-004, and that AC-015/016 golden values are derived from it deterministically.\n\nActually, let me verify whether `.collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/` has these. That's what the Explore agent would tell me. If they DO exist, this blocker is weakened (but the \"frozen before T-004\" point stands). Let me keep it but phrase carefully. Actually, I'll have the agent check.\n\n**TB-4: Characterization \"sha256 frozen files\" vs. M1/M4 rewrites of the same lib files.** AC-005 locks the 0.1 library exports via sha256 in `frozen-files.json`, and `check-frozen-files` \"在文件被修改时失败\". But T-005/T-006/T-007/T-008 (M1) and T-022 (M4) rewrite `lib/config.mjs`, `lib/forecast.mjs`, `lib/select.mjs`, `lib/cli.mjs`, etc. If the sha256 covers the LIVE lib files, every one of those tasks breaks the check. Clarify that the hash covers an immutable 0.1 fixture copy under `test/fixtures/characterization/` (and that `stable.test.mjs` runs against that copy), not the live `lib/`; otherwise the freeze contradicts the refactor plan. Also: \"保留行为\" includes \"schema 名\" and forecast behavior, but F-14/AC-067 declare semantic changes to forecast/v1 (new tasks_left_basis/risk_basis) — need to separate \"preserved\" surface from \"intentionally changed\" surface so the characterization tests don't fail on intended changes.\n\nThis is a strong, concrete blocker. Let me include it.\n\n**TB-5: AC-001 set-equality discovery vs. `--ac` filtered runs and platform-skipped files.** AC-001 asserts the enumerated `*.test.mjs` set equals the reporter's \"actually executed files\" set, and AC-004/traceability let `run-tests.mjs --ac AC-xxx` run only a subset (e.g., `node scripts/run-tests.mjs --ac AC-003`). If `check-test-discovery` (part of `npm run check` / `check-fast`) is ever run against a filtered reporter output, set equality fails. Need to define that discovery check runs only against a FULL `npm test` run's reporter, and that platform-skipped files still count as \"executed\" (node:test loads them). Also each task writes its own `test/traceability/<T>.json` shard (AC-004 merges them) — with 30 shards each listing \"全部 AC\" initially planned, the per-AC file/title assertions need a single owner; need to define how covered status is assigned to exactly one shard to avoid duplicate/contradictory coverage claims.\n\nHmm, that's two points. Let me keep the first (full-run requirement) as the blocker and mention shard ownership. Actually the design says T-001 writes \"T-001.json（列出全部 AC，初始为 planned）\" and \"每个任务写自己的 test/traceability/<T>.json 分片\". So T-001 lists ALL ACs as planned, then each task flips its own ACs to covered in its own shard? That would mean T-001.json has all as planned AND each other shard has some as covered — merging would produce duplicates/conflicts. AC-004: \"合并 test/traceability/*.json：AC 集合必须恰为 AC-001..AC-071\". If T-001.json lists all 71 as planned, and T-002.json lists AC-005 as covered, the merged set has AC-005 twice with conflicting status. This is a real inconsistency. Need to define merge semantics (e.g., shards contain ONLY their owned ACs; T-001.json is the skeleton with all planned but is REPLACED per-AC, or coverage wins over planned). \n\nActually re-reading AC-004: \"合并 ... AC 集合必须恰为 AC-001..AC-071；status 为 covered 的条目，其文件必须存在，且至少一个测试标题含对应的 [AC-xxx]；每条 AC 都声明 baseline\". \"AC 集合\" = set of AC IDs. So it's a set of IDs, not per-entry. But status conflicts need resolution. And \"每条 AC 都声明 baseline\" — baseline declared once. This is a legit ambiguity worth flagging: the merge must deduplicate with a defined precedence (covered > planned), and T-001's all-planned skeleton must not conflict. I'll fold this into TB-5 or make it its own. Let me make it TB-5 (traceability merge semantics) since it's concrete.\n\nLet me also consider:\n\n**TB-6: AC-056 / AC-011 \"call 子树必须逐项等于包装模板\" vs. AC-064 executing `calls[0]` with absolute machine-specific paths.** The wrapper template contains `<pkg>`, `<abs state-dir>`, `<abs config>` which are absolute and machine/run-specific. \"逐项等于包装模板\" requires the test to know the exact expected array. But AC-064 requires executing `calls[0]` \"原样\" in a NEW process and getting event/v1. For both to hold, the wrapper template must be parameterized and the test must compute expected values from the same `resolvePaths` (AC-012). Need to define the template as a function of (pkg root, lease id, config abs, state-dir abs) rather than a literal, and ensure the scanner's \"逐项等于\" compares against that computed template — otherwise AC-011's canary/clean-sample assertions become brittle across machines. Also: the wrapped call embeds `lease_id` (opaque) — must ensure `lease_id` and `handle_id` are not in the forbidden-value set generated \"由当前目录生成（模型 id、key、CLI 可执行名）\" — they aren't, fine.\n\nThis is more of a test-design refinement than a hard blocker. I'll consider including as a lower-priority one or fold into strategy. I'll probably keep blockers to the strongest 4-5.\n\nLet me also reconsider:\n\n**AC-047 \"只有 timeout 时 exec 计数为 2，其他都为 1\"** — \"只在超时时重试一次\" (第 7 节真实探测). So timeout → 2 exec calls (original + 1 retry). OK. But AC-028 also tests timeout with process tree kill. And AC-058 \"timeout 模式时整棵进程树被杀，返回 E_TIMEOUT\". Consistent.\n\n**AC-026 \"10 个敌意参数...在直接执行时原样传递，在 cmd 回退路径上返回 E_UNSAFE_ARG\"** and AC-027 \"带 a&b 参数的 .cmd 垫片被解析后直接用 node 执行，脚本收到的 argv 完全一致；不经 shell 直接 spawn .cmd 得到 EINVAL 的分支被捕获并转入解析路径\". So on win32, if the .cmd shim can be parsed (node + script resolved), you execute node directly with the hostile arg (argv identical, no shell). If parse fails, fall back to cmd.exe /d /s /c with arg whitelist `^[A-Za-z0-9_./:=@+,-]+$`, returning E_UNSAFE_ARG for hostile args. AC-027 says \"带 a&b 参数的 .cmd 垫片被解析后直接用 node 执行\" — so a&b passes through when parse succeeds. But AC-026 says on \"cmd 回退路径\" hostile args return E_UNSAFE_ARG. Consistent (two different paths). OK.\n\nBut hold on: AC-026 says \"10 个敌意参数...在直接执行时原样传递\" — \"直接执行\" = direct exec (shell:false, args array). The 10 hostile chars include 空格 (space), 双引号, 换行, 反引号. With shell:false and array args, these are passed literally — correct. OK.\n\nNow, let me also think about whether there's a **M1 milestone definition problem**: \"M1 基线：工程化、特征化、注入缝、契约冻结、修复 A 节全部缺陷\". But A5 defects include \"A5 无缓存 → T-022 (M4)\" (AC-055) and \"A5 shell 问题 → T-010 (M2)\" (AC-026/027). Look at 第 16 节 A 节缺陷表:\n- A5 shell → T-010 → AC-026/027 (M2)\n- A5 无缓存 → T-022 → AC-055 (M4)\n\nSo \"修复 A 节全部缺陷\" (fix ALL A-section defects) is claimed as M1's goal, but some A5 defects are fixed in M2 and M4! That's a direct contradiction between the milestone title and the defect/task mapping. From a test-architecture view: AC-005 says \"A1..A5 每条缺陷各有一个 defects/<id>.test.mjs，在 M5 结束时全部断言已修复的行为\" — so defect tests are flipped by their owning tasks across M1/M2/M4 and ALL must be green by M5. That's consistent with the table. But the M1 milestone TITLE \"修复 A 节全部缺陷\" is wrong/overclaiming. Also AC-001..AC-071 are spread across all milestones.\n\nThis is a real inconsistency worth flagging: M1's stated scope (\"修复 A 节全部缺陷\") contradicts 第 16 节 (A5-shell→T-010/M2, A5-nocache→T-022/M4) and AC-005 (\"在 M5 结束时全部断言已修复\"). Need to either reword M1 or restate the defect-flip completion at M5. This affects milestone gating and release-gate baselines (if M1 gate expects all defect tests green, it will fail). Good blocker — this is a clean structural catch.\n\nActually, this is a strong one. Let me include it.\n\nLet me also check **T-030 depends_on**: `[\"T-001\", \"T-012\", \"T-029\"]`. But T-030 outputs `test/integration/flow-complete.test.mjs` which asserts AC-071 (all 9 steps). The 9 steps are created by T-013, T-016, T-017, T-020, T-022, T-023, T-024 — none of which are direct deps of T-030. T-029 depends on T-026, T-027, T-028; T-028 depends on T-024, T-025, T-026, T-027. So transitively T-030 → T-029 → T-028 → T-024 → (T-013, T-022, T-023, T-012). And T-024 depends on T-022, T-023, T-012, T-013. T-022 depends on T-020, T-021... So transitively T-030 comes after all step-creating tasks. OK, fine, transitively sound. But it's fragile: T-030's declared depends_on omits the actual producers of the step files. A test architect would flag that dependency declarations should include the direct producers (T-013/016/017/020/022/023/024) so that a partial/parallel execution doesn't run flow-complete before steps exist. Minor but worth a note — could fold into a blocker about dependency hygiene. Actually, I'll mention it in strategy (traceability/dependency) rather than as a top blocker. Or include as a low-priority blocker. Let me keep blockers focused.\n\nLet me also double check **AC-002**: \"check-ci 校验 .github/workflows/ci.yml 是由 scripts/ci-matrix.json 生成的最新版本\". So ci.yml is GENERATED. T-001 outputs both `scripts/gen-ci.mjs` + `scripts/ci-matrix.json` + `.github/workflows/ci.yml`. AC-001 self-test places `x.test.mjs` in `test/fixtures` and asserts not executed. AC-003 injects a failing check-* step. AC-004 merged shards. OK.\n\nBut AC-003: \"node scripts/check-fast.mjs 按字母序执行 scripts/check-*.mjs（不含自身），最后执行 npm test\". So check-fast runs ALL check-*.mjs (which includes check-test-discovery, check-ci, check-traceability, check-frozen-files, check-seams, check-unused, check-no-model-table, check-pack, check-docs, check-unused...). Note check-fast.mjs would also run `check-fast.mjs`? No — \"不含自身\". But would it run `scripts/check-fast.ps1`? No, that's .ps1 not .mjs. Would it run `scripts/snapshot-update.mjs`? No, doesn't match check-*. OK. But would the injected failing step (self-test fixture) be under scripts/ permanently? It must be injected to a temp location. The design says \"自测：注入一个失败步骤，两个入口都以同一个非 0 码退出\". Need to define injection mechanism (e.g., `CLIWORKER_CHECK_DIR` override or a temp dir). Minor.\n\nHmm, one more: **AC-003 \"pwsh ... 原样传递 $LASTEXITCODE\"** vs CI on ubuntu/macos. If check-fast.ps1 is exercised in the CI matrix (each cell runs `npm run check`), and `npm run check` runs check-fast.mjs (node), not the .ps1. The .ps1 wrapper test (AC-003 self-test) requires pwsh. On GitHub runners, pwsh exists. OK. But AC-002 says \"每格运行 npm run check\". `npm run check` = ? T-001 outputs package.json scripts including `check`. Probably `node scripts/check-fast.mjs`. So the .ps1 is tested by AC-003's own integration test (which calls pwsh directly), gated by pwsh availability. If pwsh is missing on a runner, AC-003's pwsh assertion is skipped → and AC-070 says skip never counts as pass → release blocked. But pwsh is on all GH runners. OK, not a blocker. Though note the designer said \"没有 pwsh 也能跑\" for check-fast.mjs — meaning the .ps1 test might be optional. Slight tension with \"skip never counts as pass\". I'll leave it.\n\nOK. Let me also reconsider whether to include a blocker about **AC-020 \"ctx.forecast 计数器等于通过前置过滤的模型数\" vs. AC-055 \"选模过程中注入的 exec 和 fetch 计数都为 0\"** — these are different counters (forecast vs exec/fetch). Fine.\n\nAnd **AC-021 \"断言只针对拒选集合与原因，不针对排序\"** vs AC-056 \"AC-051..053 各夹具在 AgentLine 视图下的实际输出，经视图扫描器检查都是 0 命中\". So AC-051 (policy golden, full ordering) is tested in full view (admin), but AC-056 says AC-051..053 fixtures in AgentLine view scan 0 hits. But AgentLine view only has opaque handle_ids and call — does it even have ordering? The policy golden asserts \"输出顺序与 expected 深相