he CI matrix.** Define report→gate path and exemptions; AC-038 also declares levels=integration but baseline=smoke (inconsistent).\n\n- **TB-5 (open): External \"interfaces\"/\"B.4.4\" spec is the oracle for the frozen registry but is not a committed, versioned artifact in the task graph.** T-004 must freeze against a stable in-repo spec; otherwise AC-010 snapshot comparison and AC-015/016 goldens have no fixed oracle. (I'll verify with the Explore agent whether these files exist; if they do, I'll soften to \"must be frozen/versioned before T-004\".)\n\n- **TB-6 (open, maybe): Traceability shard merge semantics.** T-001.json lists all 71 as planned; each task writes its own shard with covered ACs; AC-004 merges to a set of exactly 71. Need defined dedup/precedence (covered > planned), single owner per AC+file+title, and that T-001 skeleton is superseded — otherwise duplicate/conflicting statuses. Also T-030 depends_on omits the direct producers of the 9 flow steps.\n\nHmm, that's 6. The user said blockers is an array; no limit. But I should keep it focused and high-value. I'll include maybe 5-6. Let me include 5 strong ones and possibly fold TB-6 into strategy. Actually TB-6 (traceability merge) is concrete and real. Let me include 5 or 6. I'll go with 5 strongest + maybe the traceability one. Let me do 5: TB-1..TB-5, and mention traceability merge + dependency hygiene inside the strategy (as a design note) OR as TB-6. \n\nI think I'll do 6 but keep each terse. Actually, quality over quantity — a test architect should surface only genuine blockers. Let me include 5. I'll fold the traceability merge concern into TB-5 or into the strategy. Hmm, let me reconsider: which are truly \"blockers\" (things that must be resolved before implementation can proceed soundly) vs. refinements?\n\nAll 5-6 are genuine. I'll include 5 (TB-1 through TB-5) and add the traceability/dependency point as TB-6 because it directly affects AC-004/AC-070 gating correctness. Actually, let me mer