ign artifacts of 'CLIWorker v2'. I need to know whether an authoritative 'interfaces' specification document exists (the redesign references 'interfaces 第 1～15 节', 'interfaces 第 6～8 节', 'interfaces 第 11 节', 'interfaces 第 2 节' as the source for error codes, exit codes, risk threshold tables, quota-shape normalization, and pool/forecast formulas) and whether 'B.4.4' (a quota golden reference) exists. Also check for 'review-v1' and any 'registry.snapshot.json' or 'contracts/' directory. List every file found under .collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/ with a one-line description of what it contains, and quote the section headings of any interfaces doc. Also check whether contracts/, docs/, ui/, test/ directories currently exist at repo root. Report concisely. Do not modify anything.\"\n\nThese are good, focused. Let me launch both in parallel.\n\nWait — should I worry that launching Explore agents might be \"over-engineering\" given the user wants a quick JSON output? I think the grounding is worth it and it's consistent with the plan mode's Phase 1. Let me do it but keep it to 2 agents, quick.\n\nActually, the system reminder says Phase 1 \"Critical: In this phase you should only use the Explore subagent type\" and \"Launch up to 3 Explore agents IN PARALLEL\". So 2 Explore agents in parallel is exactly aligned. Good. Let me do that.\n\nAfter that, Phase 2 says launch a Plan agent. But given this is a pure analysis deliverable (not an implementation plan), and the user forbids file creation, I'll skip the Plan agent and directly synthesize. I'll note that I'm honoring the read-only JSON deliverable. Actually — hmm, the plan mode workflow is fairly insistent. But I've decided to prioritize the user's explicit request. I'll proceed with the 2 Explore agents then output the JSON.\n\nLet me launch.","signature":""}],"model":"hy4-free","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tok