{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b5c8-4d0d-760b-bf7a-3f58febf9707","session_id":"01a1b5bf-5519-7a7b-8d8d-80d1042af7bf","message":{"id":"01a1b5c84d0d760bbf7a3f566c8f8549","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Bash is denied. That's fine — I have enough from the agents. I won't work around it. I can't verify git tracking directly, but the agent's report from `logs/designer.log:102` says `.collab/` was untracked at round 1. I'll phrase the blocker carefully without overclaiming.\n\nNow let me think about the round-1 blockers status relative to the new design:\n\nRound-1 TB-1 (injectable seams) → RESOLVED by F-01/T-003 (M1). \nTB-2 (undefined formulas/oracle) → RESOLVED by F-03 (§6-8 in interfaces + registry, unique expected values).\nTB-3 (wall-clock thresholds) → RESOLVED by F-04 (structural invariants, perf separate, file barriers, ci-matrix).\nTB-4 (toolchain gap: lockfile, scripts, devDep, pwsh) → RESOLVED by F-04 (lockfile), F-13 (no devDependency, narrow lexical check-unused), pwsh confirmed 7.6.9.\nTB-5 (cross-platform skip) → RESOLVED by F-11 (platform-gate, skips.jsonl, baseline, skip never = pass).\nTB-6 (contract not frozen → rework) → RESOLVED by F-02/第0节第1条 (freeze to M1/T-004, snapshot).\nTB-7 (design errata) → RESOLVED by 第2节勘误 (designer corrected all four).\nTB-8 (cumulative harness no single owner) → RESOLVED by F-10 (shared leak-scan.mjs, flow steps auto-discovered, canary, every npm test reruns).\nTB-9 (release gate semantics) → RESOLVED by F-11/AC-070 (skip blocks, dry-run, report sanitization).\nTB-10 (level/dir/traceability misalignment) → RESOLVED by F-16/第15节 (level→dir mapping, per-task shards, set-equality).\nTB-11/12/13 → already resolved.\n\nSo ALL round-1 blockers are addressed by the second-round design. That's actually a KEY insight for my strategy: the second revision is a systematic closure of all 10 open round-1 testability blockers + 16 review findings. My job as test architect in this round is to VERIFY that closure and surface any NEW/residual blockers.\n\nSo my strategy should explicitly state: round-1 TB-1..TB-10 are now closed (mapped to the design's fixes), and I've re-audited the round-2 design for residual issues. Then list the NEW blockers I found.\n\nThis is much more valuable than a generic strategy. Let me restructure.\n\nNow, NEW blockers specific to round 2 (my findings):\n\n**TB-1 (new): M1 milestone scope contradicts A-section defect ownership.**\nM1 title: \"基线：工程化、特征化、注入缝、契约冻结、修复 A 节全部缺陷\". But 第16节 A 节缺陷表 maps:\n- A5 shell → T-010 (M2) → AC-026/027\n- A5 无缓存 → T-022 (M4) → AC-055\nAnd AC-005: \"A1..A5 每条缺陷各有一个 defects/<id>.test.mjs，在 M5 结束时全部断言已修复的行为\". So defect tests are flipped across M1/M2/M4 and all green at M5. If M1 gate / release-gate treats \"A 节全部缺陷\" as an M1 exit criterion, it fails. Need to reword M1 and fix the milestone-gate definition; also AC-005's \"M5 结束时\" must be the authoritative completion point so no milestone prematurely asserts all defect files green.\n\n**TB-2 (new): `now` seam must be an advanceable/mutable clock, not merely a fixed value.**\nT-003 `ctx` specifies \"固定时钟\"; check-seams only bans bare `Date.now`/`new Date` outside `lib/context.mjs`. But ~9 ACs require advancing time within one test process while the design forbids wall-clock sleep (\"用文件屏障代替 sleep\", \"注入时钟加屏障，不用 sleep\", AC-028 \"不断言墙钟时间\"): AC-019 (now > reset_at → used_fraction 归零), AC-028 (lock_wait_ms 超时), AC-029 (lock_stale_ms、窗口过期), AC-047 (callable 过 TTL → availability_stale), AC-049 (读数超过 reading_ttl_s → W_STALE_DATA), AC-058 (过期租约 E_LEASE_EXPIRED), AC-064 (count=3 三个租约按顺序执行不过期，\"在注入时钟下\"), AC-064/第0节第6条 (expires_at 按 i×timeout_s 递延). Need to pin in T-003/contracts/host: a settable/advanceable clock API (`ctx.now()` reading a mutable value + `ctx.clock.advance(ms)` / `setNow(t)`), and that ALL production modules read time only via `ctx.now()`. Otherwise these ACs are untestable without sleeps → flaky or fake-pass.\n\n**TB-3 (new): Characterization sha256 scope vs. M1/M4 rewrites of the same lib files + intentional semantic changes.**\nAC-005 locks \"0.1 的库导出\" via sha256 in `frozen-files.json`, and `check-frozen-files` \"在文件被修改时失败\". But T-005/T-006/T-007/T-008 (M1) and T-022 (M4) rewrite `lib/config.mjs`, `lib/forecast.mjs`, `lib/select.mjs`, `lib/cli.mjs`, `lib/index.js` — the very files. If the hash covers live `lib/`, every one of those tasks breaks the check. Must clarify: hash covers an immutable 0.1 fixture copy under `test/fixtures/characterization/`, and `stable.test.mjs` runs against that copy (not live lib). Additionally, \"保留行为\" includes \"schema 名\" and forecast behavior, but F-14/AC-067 declare intentional semantic changes to forecast/v1 (new `tasks_left_basis`, `risk_basis`, draft→v1 mapping) and config schema v1→v2. Need an explicit preserved-surface vs. intentionally-changed-surface split so characterization tests don't fail on intended changes; otherwise T-002's locked assertions conflict with T-006/T-014.\n\n**TB-4 (new): Release-gate \"every AC must pass on baseline; skip never = pass\" is unsatisfiable for native/smoke-baselined ACs outside the 3-OS CI matrix.**\nAC-070: \"每条 AC 都必须在它的基线平台上至少有一次 pass；skip 永远不算 pass\". AC-027 baseline win32 (satisfiable on windows runner). But AC-038 baseline is \"smoke，由真机 smoke 的 wsl-discover 步骤承担\" — its `levels` is `[\"integration\"]` yet baseline is `smoke` (inconsistent), and WSL-with-distro is not on ubuntu/windows/macos runners; real smoke runs only under `CLIWORKER_SMOKE=1` by a maintainer (T-029/AC-069). T-030's inputs list \"CI 产物、smoke 报告、traceability、flow steps\" but its outputs/acceptance_direction never define how a real-smoke pass is CREDITED to an AC's baseline, nor which ACs are exempt. Without a defined report→gate data path, either the gate permanently blocks or AC-038 is structurally unpassable in CI. Need: (a) baseline declared consistently with levels; (b) explicit list of native-only ACs and the artifact (real-smoke report) that supplies their baseline pass; (c) release-gate parsing that maps report entries to AC IDs; or a documented exemption rule.\n\n**TB-5 (new): The frozen-registry oracle lives in `.collab/` — untracked, excluded from the package, single-line, and not versioned with `contracts/`.**\nT-004's input is \"interfaces 第 1～15 节\"; AC-016's golden is \"B.4.4 金标\" from the original requirement. Grounding check: `interfaces.md` and `designer.log`/`state.json` (B.4.4) exist ONLY under `.collab/blueprint/cliworker-v2/`, which round-1 logs show was untracked, `.gitignore` does not ignore it (so it's not even intentionally excluded — it's just not committed), and AC-025 explicitly requires `npm pack` to NOT contain `.collab/`. A CI checkout (fresh clone) therefore has no `interfaces.md`/B.4.4, while T-004 must enumerate \"全部码与枚举\" and AC-010/AC-015/016 goldens are derived from those sections. Need to promote the authoritative spec into a versioned, in-repo, machine-readable artifact under `contracts/` (or absorb it into `registry.snapshot.json` + `docs/contract.md`, which T-004 does output), and make `registry.snapshot.json` SELF-CONTAINING (no runtime read of `.collab/`). Also AC-025's pack check must not accidentally depend on `.collab/` at test time.\n\nHmm — is TB-5 fully fair? The design DOES output `docs/contract.md` from T-004. And AC-009 says registry.mjs deep-equals registry.snapshot.json — self-contained. And AC-010 uses compareRegistry with a registry COPY. So the actual tests are self-contained. The risk is only about the INPUT to T-004 and the derivation of golden values. And about \"冻结规则\" needing a stable oracle. I think it's still a legitimate blocker but I should phrase it as \"the oracle must be promoted/versioned\", acknowledging T-004's docs/contract.md output as the intended home but flagging that `.collab/` being untracked+pack-excluded means a fresh CI clone lacks the source. That's real.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to include TB-5 or replace it with the traceability-merge one. Both are real. Let me think about which is more valuable/defensible.\n\nTB-5 is grounded in concrete filesystem findings — strong. But there's a counter: the blueprint artifacts are \"process artifacts\" that live in `.collab/` by design, and the task graph is the authoritative input (the user just gave it to me in the prompt). The design text itself (provided inline) contains all the formulas (§9), threshold tables, etc. So actually the DESIGN (§9 etc.) is the spec, and `interfaces.md` is a supporting doc. Hmm. The design §9 fully specifies the formulas. So the \"interfaces\" doc is somewhat redundant with the design itself. But T-004's input explicitly says \"interfaces 第 1～15 节\" — so SOMETHING must be authoritative. If that something is untracked, there's a versioning gap.\n\nI'll include it but phrase precisely and not overclaim (\"verified on disk under `.collab/`; round-1 logs indicate untracked; `.gitignore` does not list it; AC-025 excludes `.collab/` from the package\"). I'll ask for it to be promoted/versioned, not claim it's definitely broken.\n\n**TB-6 (new): Traceability shard merge semantics + T-030 dependency omissions.**\nAC-004: \"合并 test/traceability/*.json：AC 集合必须恰为 AC-001..AC-071\". T-001 outputs \"T-001.json（列出全部 AC，初始为 planned）\"; F-11/第15节 \"每个任务写自己的 test/traceability/<T>.json 分片\". If T-001.json lists all 71 as `planned` and each later shard flips its ACs to `covered`, a naive merge yields duplicate AC IDs with conflicting status, and two shards could both claim `[AC-xxx]` titles. Need defined merge precedence (`covered` > `planned`), exactly one owning shard per AC (file + `[AC-xxx]` title + baseline), and T-001's skeleton to be demoted/superseded. Related: T-030 declares `depends_on: [T-001, T-012, T-029]` but AC-071 asserts the 9-step flow set, whose direct producers are T-013/016/017/020/022/023/024 — none declared as direct deps (only transitively via T-029→T-028→T-024). For parallel/partial execution, declare direct producers so flow-complete never runs before the steps exist; also `check-test-discovery` (AC-001 set-equality) must run only against a FULL `npm test` reporter, never a `--ac` filtered run (AC-003/AC-004 use `run-tests.mjs --ac AC-xxx`).\n\nThis is a solid 6th blocker. \n\nLet me also double-check one thing: is `AC-038` really `levels: [\"integration\"]` with baseline smoke? Yes: \n```\n\"id\": \"AC-038\",\n\"text\": \"原生 WSL 枚举（win32 且装有 WSL 时运行，否则写跳过记录）：... baseline 为 smoke，由真机 smoke 的 wsl-discover 步骤承担。\",\n\"levels\": [\"integration\"]\n```\nYes. And AC-069 smoke dry-run steps are: 发现、枚举、探测、选模、run 极小提示、http-select — no \"wsl-discover\" step! AC-038 says \"由真机 smoke 的 wsl-discover 步骤承担\", but AC-069's dry-run steps don't include wsl-discover, and T-029's outputs (`scripts/smoke-real.mjs`, `test/smoke/**`, `docs/release-checklist.md`) don't mention a wsl-discover step. And AC-071's 9 flows steps don't include wsl-discover. So the \"wsl-discover step\" that AC-038 relies on **does not exist in any task's outputs**. That's an even stronger, concrete gap! Let me verify AC-069: \"smoke-real --dry-run 在 fake-cli 环境下运行：步骤依次为发现、枚举、探测、选模、run 极小提示、http-select，全部 pass\". No wsl-discover. And real smoke (non-dry-run) \"由维护者在真机运行\" — no step list defined. So AC-038's baseline pass has NO defined producer. Strong.\n\nAlso, AC-038's `levels` [\"integration\"] but T-016's write_scope includes `test/integration/discovery-wsl-native.test.mjs` and AC-038 is in T-016's acceptance [\"AC-036\",\"AC-037\",\"AC-038\",\"AC-039\",\"AC-040\"]. So T-016 DOES produce a native WSL integration test. So there IS a test file. But its baseline is declared as \"smoke\" rather than \"win32\", and the text says the pass is \"由真机 smoke 的 wsl-discover 步骤承担\" — which contradicts the existence of `discovery-wsl-native.test.mjs`. Confusing. Either way, baseline declaration is inconsistent and the smoke step doesn't exist. I'll fold this into TB-4 with both points.\n\nGood. Let me also reconsider: is TB-1 (M1 scope) truly a \"blocker\"? It's a milestone-title/scope inconsistency. From a test-architecture view, if release-gate or milestone gates are derived from the milestone titles, it breaks. It's a real spec inconsistency worth flagging. I'll keep it but rank it appropriately (it's lower severity than the clock seam). Actually, I'll order by severity: TB-2 (clock) and TB-4 (release gate natively unpassable) and TB-3 (frozen files) are the most test-breaking. Then TB-1, TB-5, TB-6.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider TB-3 more. Actually the design says \"stable.test.mjs 通过 0.1 的库导出（selectModels、listModels、forecast、estimateCost）锁定保留行为\". \"0.1 的库导出\" could mean \"the 0.1 library's exports\" — i.e., a snapshot of the 0.1 library. And \"其 sha256 记录在 test/characterization/frozen-files.json\" — \"其\" = the 0.1 library exports/snapshot. \"check-frozen-files 在文件被修改时失败\". I think the INTENT is indeed to hash a frozen COPY (a 0.1 snapshot fixture). T-002's write_scope includes `test/fixtures/characterization/**` — so there IS a fixture dir for the frozen 0.1 copy! That supports my reading: the hash covers `test/fixtures/characterization/` (the frozen 0.1 lib copy), not live lib. So TB-3's first half might already be handled by design intent. But it's ambiguous enough (\"在文件被修改时失败\" — WHICH files?) that it needs explicit clarification. And the second half (preserved vs. intentionally-changed surface) is definitely a real gap: AC-005 lists \"schema 名\" as preserved behavior, but config schema changes v1→v2 (AC-034, W_CONFIG_V1) and forecast/v1 adds fields (F-14). Hmm — \"schema 名\" might refer to output schema names like `cliworker.selection/v1` vs draft, not config schema. Actually AC-005 says \"锁定保留行为（弃用和未验证模型不入候选、等级过滤、exclude 的原因、schema 名）\". \"schema 名\" likely means the output schema name (e.g., `cliworker.selection/draft/v1`), which should be preserved. OK, so maybe no conflict there.\n\nLet me soften TB-3: focus on the ambiguity of WHICH files the sha256 covers (must be the immutable 0.1 fixture copy under `test/fixtures/characterization/`, never live `lib/`, since T-005/006/007/008/022 rewrite those), and the need to define that `stable.test.mjs` runs against the frozen copy while defect files assert the LIVE evolving lib. If the hash covers live lib, 5+ tasks break `check-frozen-files`. That's a genuine, concrete clarification blocker. I'll keep it but phrase as \"must be pinned explicitly\".\n\nActually, I realize there might be an even more concrete issue: `check-frozen-files` is run by `check-fast.mjs` (alphabetical `check-*.mjs`) at every `npm run check` and `npm test` (AC-003: check-fast runs all check-*.mjs then npm test). If it hashes live lib files, then from T-005 onward, EVERY `npm test` fails. So it MUST hash the fixture copy. Definitely worth pinning. Good blocker.\n\nAlright. Let me also reconsider whether to include TB-5 (external oracle). Given the design §9 fully specifies formulas inline and T-004 outputs docs/contract.md + registry.snapshot.json, maybe the `.collab/interfaces.md` issue is lower priority. But it's a real versioning/availability gap. I'll keep it but rank last-ish, or merge into TB-6. Let me keep 6 blockers — thorough is good for a test architect. Actually, let me reconsider: too many blockers can dilute. The user gave a very thorough design and expects a thorough test architect review. 6 well-grounded blockers is fine. But let me make sure each is genuinely \"open\" and not something the design already handles.\n\nLet me re-examine each against the design text one final time:\n\n1. M1 scope vs A5 defects in M2/M4 — design AC-005 says \"在 M5 结束时全部断言已修复的行为\", and 第16节 table clearly puts A5-shell→T-010/M2 and A5-nocache→T-022/M4. M1 title says \"修复 A 节全部缺陷\". **Genuine contradiction.** ✓\n\n2. Advanceable clock — T-003 \"固定时钟\", check-seams bans bare Date.now outside context.mjs. No explicit advanceable clock API. Many ACs need time travel + \"不用 sleep\". **Genuine gap.** ✓ Strong.\n\n3. Frozen-files hash scope — ambiguous, must pin to fixture copy. **Genuine clarification needed.** ✓\n\n4. Release gate baseline for native/smoke ACs (AC-038), including missing wsl-discover step. **Genuine.** ✓ Strong.\n\n5. `.collab/interfaces.md` oracle versioning/availability in CI. **Genuine but partially mitigated by docs/contract.md + self-contained snapshot.** I'll keep it, phrased carefully. Moderate.\n\n6. Traceability merge precedence + T-030 direct-dependency omission + discovery check only on full runs. **Genuine.** ✓\n\nOK. I might drop #5 to keep focus, OR keep it. Given the user is a \"test architect\" review and the grounding found `.collab/` untracked + AC-025 excludes it, I think it's a valuable, non-obvious catch. Keep all 6.\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider #5 once more. Is it really a blocker for TESTING? The tests (AC-009, AC-010, AC-015, AC-016) all use self-contained fixtures (`contracts/examples/`, `test/fixtures/forecast/*.json`, `registry.snapshot.json`). AC-016 \"B.4.4 金标\" gives explicit expected values inline in AC text (2/10, 1/5, 1.8/9, 0.8/4). So the golden values ARE in the task graph itself. `interfaces.md` is an INPUT to implementation (T-004), not to tests. So from a pure TEST perspective, the tests are fine. The risk is more about implementation/spec drift. Hmm. That weakens #5 as a TEST blocker.\n\nBut the user is \"测试架构师\" and the blockers are \"阻塞说明\" (blocking explanations) — they can cover anything that blocks the test strategy from being sound. A frozen registry whose authoritative spec is untracked IS a testability/versioning concern (AC-010's \"删除或改名会让测试失败\" needs a stable oracle; AC-067 requires every `semantic_change` registry item to have a doc paragraph — that requires the registry to enumerate semantic changes, which requires knowing the v1→v2 deltas, which come from interfaces.md). I'll keep it but frame it in test terms: the freeze/compare/semantic-change-doc tests need a versioned oracle, and `.collab/` is untracked + pack-excluded.\n\nAct