{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a1b60b-5f69-7b66-b83c-a1aaa4d29930","session_id":"01a1b60b-5bf4-794d-89f3-197962d26440","message":{"id":"01a1b60b5f697b66b83ca1a7adfc5c1c","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to act as a test architect (test_architect) for a project called Blueprint. This is a read-only discussion. They've provided a third-round revised design document for CLIWorker v2, along with a task graph. They want me to output ONLY a single JSON object (no code block markers) with:\n\n{\"strategy\":\"测试策略正文\",\"blockers\":[{\"id\":\"TB-1\",\"status\":\"open\",\"text\":\"阻塞说明\"}]}\n\nSo I need to:\n1. Analyze the design as a test architect\n2. Produce a test strategy\n3. Identify any blockers (testability issues)\n\nLet me carefully understand the context. This is a plan-mode session but the user explicitly says \"这是只读讨论：不要修改、创建或删除任何文件\" (this is a read-only discussion: don't modify, create or delete any files). And they want only a JSON output.\n\nWait - I'm in plan mode. The system reminder says I should follow the plan workflow. But the user's request is actually a \"read-only discussion\" where they want me to act as a test architect and produce a JSON verdict. This is a bit different from the standard plan mode implementation task.\n\nLet me think carefully. The user is asking me to be a \"test architect\" and produce a review/strategy output in a specific JSON format. This appears to be part of a multi-agent workflow where different \"roles\" review design documents. The output format `{\"strategy\":..., \"blockers\":[...]}` is a verdict-style output.\n\nThis is NOT an implementation task. It's a review/analysis task. The user wants me to:\n- Analyze the design from a test architecture perspective\n- Provide a test strategy\n- Identify blockers (testability problems)\n\nThe mention of \"Blueprint\" and \"test_architect\" suggests this is a simulated review process. The previous rounds were \"review-v2\" with 8 opinions (F-01..F-08